Given the following forecast for KEC (base year 2022):
{
  "strategy": "baseline",
  "base_year": 2022,
  "forecast": [
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 17868.0,
      "net_income_cr": 384.2,
      "eps": 14.95
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 20673.0,
      "net_income_cr": 444.6,
      "eps": 17.29
    },
    {
      "year": 2025,
      "revenue_cr": 23918.8,
      "net_income_cr": 514.6,
      "eps": 20.02
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "From the consolidated P&L, Revenue from Operations was approximately 15,420 crore in FY2022 vs ~13,673 crore in FY2021 (implying ~15.7% YoY growth), while consolidated Net Income (PAT attributable to equity shareholders) was 332.08 crore in FY2022 vs 552.72 crore in FY2021 \u2014 a decline of ~40% YoY driven by margin pressures and SAE subsidiary losses. However, the sharp PAT decline in FY2022 appears to be a one-off due to commodity cost headwinds and SAE Brazil losses; applying the FY2022 revenue growth rate of ~15.7% forward for revenue, and a mean-reversion assumption for net income using a modest recovery of ~15.7% growth from the depressed FY2022 base of 332.08 crore, gives the projected figures above. Shares outstanding remain at 257,088,370 (25.71 crore shares) as reported for both FY2021 and FY2022."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

RESPONSE FORMAT: Begin your response DIRECTLY with the opening brace { — no reasoning or text before the JSON.

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "company": "<COMPANY>",
  "base_year": <YYYY>,
  "strategy": "<baseline|alt_strategy>",
  "assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "<text>", "failure_scenario": "<text>", "risk": "<Low|Medium|High>"}
  ],
  "confidence_score": <0-100>,
  "overall_critique": "<2 sentences>"
}

